+# G05 source availability audit — RUN245
+
+## Scope and disposition
+
+Reviewed all 280 rows in `G05_ACTIONS_NEEDING_SOURCE_REVIEW.csv` by cited source book. The audit records whether the cited PDF is present and what its extracted text can support. It does not approve G05 closure and does not attest mechanics from an index entry.
+
+| Disposition | Rows | Source book | Result |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| `SOURCE_FILE_AVAILABLE_TEXT_INCOMPLETE` | 131 | Monster Manual (2025) | A matching revised-edition PDF is accessible under a different Drive filename. Document identity is verified; action-by-action page validation remains incomplete because the OCR extraction distorts rules text. |
+| `EXCLUDED_NO_SOURCE` | 149 | Ravenloft: The Horrors Within | No exact or verifiable source PDF was found among the 256 direct items returned from the supplied D&D5e folder. |
+| **Total** | **280** |  | **0 rows have action semantics attested by this audit.** |
+
+## Monster Manual (2025)
+
+- Drive folder: `13wB-KfYCe2k5xGmb-z2D09KRDJtSyfHu`
+- Accessible PDF: `Manual dos Monstros 2024.pdf`, Drive file ID `1iqPMW_ljJPWZMs3jYVUagceeZ6xe7N9o`, size 277,647,654 bytes.
+- [Drive file](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1iqPMW_ljJPWZMs3jYVUagceeZ6xe7N9o/view)
+- Google Drive readable-text fetch succeeded. The extracted front matter identifies the printed title `MONSTER MANUAL`, copyright `©2025 Wizards of the Coast LLC`, and includes a “2025 Equivalent” section. Thus the internal document text supports the 2025 revised Monster Manual edition even though the filename says “2024”.
+- Extraction length: 1,066,072 characters. OCR is not reliable for exhaustive rules validation: for example, in the Bugbear Warrior entry, `Grab` appears as `Grob` and `Grappled` as `Crappled`. Its TOC lists Bugbear Warrior on printed p. 62, which is an entry locator only. I do not treat that TOC or OCR ambiguity as action evidence.
+- Disposition for all 131 rows: `SOURCE_FILE_AVAILABLE_TEXT_INCOMPLETE`. The file and edition are identified, but the action, DC, save ability, rider, trigger budget, and effect semantics are not attested row by row. Page references remain `NOT_VERIFIED_PER_ROW`, except the Bugbear Warrior locator noted above.
+
+## Ravenloft: The Horrors Within
+
+- Drive folder: `13wB-KfYCe2k5xGmb-z2D09KRDJtSyfHu`
+- `google_drive_list_folder` with `top_k=1000` returned 256 direct items; none is the cited book or a verifiable PDF of it. No Drive file ID exists for the requested source in this folder inventory.
+- The only directly listed Ravenloft-titled PDF is `Dominus & Dragons - Ravenloft - Capa Preta.pdf` (ID `1VoLhLrrKZWxP6DBjHogBDllMHMd_emFe`, 308,505 bytes). Its extracted title identifies a Dominus & Dragons solo-RPG campaign module, not the cited bestiary.
+- A Drive text search for the Ankhtepot action surfaced `fddh.pdf` (ID `1-vr-YT-5KkE0Mcq4YxFTItMDIJZtVju4`). Its front matter identifies `Statistics for 16 Darklords at All Tiers of Play`, ©2021 by Wyatt Trull. This is a different work and is not accepted as a substitute for the cited book.
+- Disposition for all 149 rows: `EXCLUDED_NO_SOURCE`; exact source edition and page/action cannot be confirmed. The Drive folder ID and exact absence/candidate details are repeated in the CSV for every affected row.
+
+## Impact
+
+The 149 Ravenloft rows cannot proceed to source validation without the exact source PDF. The 131 Monster Manual rows have an accessible edition-matched PDF but remain mechanically unverified at row level because OCR is ambiguous; this audit does not resolve DCs, abilities, riders, action budgets, or typed effects. G05 remains open. No motor or Android code was changed.
