+Checkout: `/workspace/braseiro-agent-d`  
+Branch: `codex/g05-qa-ci`  
+Base: RUN245 G05 source checkpoint, commit `134c382`.
+
+## Runner and toolchain observed
+
+- Managed environment: connected; observations current; HTTP policy `unrestricted`, state `enforced`.
+- `/etc/codex/network-policy.json`: HTTP sidecar proxy `http://proxy:8080`; VPN not configured; no TCP grants. `HTTP_PROXY` and `HTTPS_PROXY` are set in the process environment. No credentials or environment values were printed.
+- Java: OpenJDK `21.0.12.1`, runtime home `/usr/lib/jvm/java-21-openjdk-amd64`.
+- `javac` is not on `PATH`; the `jdk.compiler` module is present and can be invoked with `java --module jdk.compiler/com.sun.tools.javac.Main`.
+- Project wrapper: Gradle `8.11.1`, matching `gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties`. No system `gradle` binary was found. Wrapper distribution was downloaded into `/home/agent/.gradle`; cache grew to about `1.1G` after Gradle plugin resolution/configuration.
+- Android SDK: unavailable. `ANDROID_HOME` and `ANDROID_SDK_ROOT` are unset; `adb` and `sdkmanager` are absent; no `local.properties`, Android SDK platform, or `android.jar` was found in the checked locations. Project requests `compileSdk = 35`.
+- Local checkout has no `origin` remote and no checked-in `.github/workflows` directory. No workflow was dispatched.
+- The source has 17 JUnit test classes and 39 `@Test` methods under `app/src/test/java/com/braseiro/dnd5e`; three classes are RUN244/RUN245 G05 integration tests.
+
+## Executed checks
+
+| Check | Command | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| RUN244 source wiring assertions | `python3 G05_EVIDENCE/test_run244_wiring.py` | PASS, 9 assertions; explicitly source-only |
+| RUN245 source wiring assertions | `python3 G05_EVIDENCE/test_run245_wiring.py` | PASS, 15 assertions; explicitly not Android/Robolectric |
+| RUN245 pure JVM harness | `java --module jdk.compiler/com.sun.tools.javac.Main -d <tmpdir> app/src/main/java/com/braseiro/dnd5e/MonsterForcedMovementRules.java G05_EVIDENCE/Run245ForcedMovementPureHarness.java` then `java -cp <tmpdir> Run245ForcedMovementPureHarness` | PASS, 13 checks |
+| Wrapper version | `GRADLE_OPTS='-Dhttps.proxyHost=proxy -Dhttps.proxyPort=8080 -Dhttp.proxyHost=proxy -Dhttp.proxyPort=8080' ./gradlew --version` | PASS, Gradle 8.11.1 on Java 21 |
+| Android/Robolectric suite | `GRADLE_OPTS='-Dhttps.proxyHost=proxy -Dhttps.proxyPort=8080 -Dhttp.proxyHost=proxy -Dhttp.proxyPort=8080' ./gradlew --no-daemon :app:testDebugUnitTest --stacktrace` | BLOCKED before task execution: `SDK location not found`; 0 of 39 test methods ran |
+
+The initial wrapper invocation without Java proxy properties failed with `java.net.ConnectException: Connection refused` while Java attempted a direct connection. A `curl` probe through the inherited proxy reached the Gradle distribution host (`HTTP_CODE=200`). Supplying proxy system properties through command-scoped `GRADLE_OPTS` let the wrapper download and launch; this does not alter project configuration.
+
+The Gradle test task configured far enough to identify the concrete Android SDK blocker, but did not compile project sources or run Robolectric. No Android/Robolectric pass is claimed.
+
+Full captured outputs are in this directory: `static-run244.log`, `static-run245.log`, `run245-pure-jvm.log`, `http-proxy-probe.log`, `gradle-version.log`, and `gradle-robolectric.log`.
+
+## Read-only BRELGA inspection
+
+GitHub read-only inspection found repository `bra83/braseirobuild`. Its historical `.github/workflows/dnd-run229-g05-brelga.yml` and `.github/workflows/dnd-run230-brelga-android.yml` configure `runs-on: [self-hosted, Windows, X64]`. The RUN230 job has an additional runtime guard that aborts unless `RUNNER_NAME` is `BRELGA`, then runs `:app:compileDebugJavaWithJavac`, `:app:testDebugUnitTest`, and `:app:assembleDebug`. Its status text explicitly records `G05_COMPLETE=NO`.
+
+These files establish labels configured in historical workflows, not current runner availability or health. The approved read-only connector did not expose a live runner inventory endpoint. No RUN245-specific workflow was found in the repository's indexed default-branch files. I did not dispatch a workflow, create an APK, inspect secrets, or change any workflow.
